The data tables of this package come from the Unicode Character Database.

The Unicode Character Database files carry the Unicode License. The
license covers the data files and the software of the Unicode
Consortium. The license text is at
https://www.unicode.org/license.txt

The tables are built by the scripts under test/. Each script reads the
files of the Unicode Character Database 18.0.0 and writes numbers only
into the package.

The files of the security data of the standard hold the confusable
table and the identifier profile. The release 18.0.0 holds both. The
whole script table comes from the release 8.0.0, because the Unicode
Consortium stopped publishing that file after that release. The scripts
read those files and write numbers only into the package.

