The UTF-16 test vectors come from the Go, the Node and the Rust
libraries. The UTF-32 test vectors come from the codecs of Python. The
scripts write numbers only. The source code of those libraries is under
the licenses of those projects.

The scripts check each table against a second source. The second source
is the Go standard library, the Go packages golang.org/x/text/unicode/norm,
golang.org/x/text/width and golang.org/x/text/unicode/bidi, the package
golang.org/x/text/cases, the ICU library, Node with ICU and the
unicodedata module of Python. The scripts fail when the sources differ.
The ICU library 79.1 holds Unicode 18.0.0, and it judges every code point.
The Go packages and Node hold Unicode 17.0.0, so they judge the code
points that 18.0.0 did not add. The scripts use the unicodedata module as
a second check only, because it holds Unicode 16.0.0.

The width tables and the width test vectors come from the Rust
unicode-width crate 0.2.3 and from the files of the Character Database.
The crate is under the MIT license and the Apache License 2.0. The
script test/make_width_data.py reads the crate through the oracle in
test/oracle and writes numbers only. No source code of the crate is in
this package.

The sentence break exceptions of the seven locales come from the ICU
library, release 79.1, source tree icu4c/source/data/brkitr: en.txt,
de.txt, es.txt, fr.txt, it.txt, pt.txt and ru.txt. The files carry the
Unicode License. The script test/make_sent_abbr_data.py reads the lists
and writes trie numbers only into the package. No list file itself is in
this package.

The five word lists of the dictionary word segmentation come from the
ICU library, release 79.1, source tree
icu4c/source/data/brkitr/dictionaries: thaidict.txt, khmerdict.txt,
laodict.txt, burmesedict.txt and cjdict.txt. The lists carry the
Unicode License and the licenses of their original word list sources,
which the headers of the files name. The script test/make_dict_data.py
reads the lists and writes trie numbers only into the package. No word
list file itself is in this package.

The cases of the paragraph and line calls come from the ICU library,
release 79.1, and from the Rust crate unicode-bidi 0.3.18. The crate is
under the MIT license and the Apache License 2.0. The script
test/make_bidi_line_cases.py reads both through the oracles in
test/oracle and writes numbers only. No source code of the crate and no
source code of the library is in this package.
